Changes made for this contribution:
  - Import paths redirected to kernel-compiled W11 supporting modules.
  - Namespaces moved under ZInQ.Contrib.CloudB3W11TateTrace, except the
    shared, genuine PadicComplex.IsTateTrace/towerClosure API.
  - P2M.Util and all P2M metaprogramming removed. Ordinary declarations and
    attributes replace the alias/export/scoped-activation plumbing.
  - Local notation inlined. Superscript-units types written explicitly.
  - The whole-group theorem stated with the local cyclotomicCharacter on
    PadicAlgCl p; irrelevant global-Qbar transport removed.
  - Lean 4.35 compatibility adjustments, notably the closure-inclusion proof.
  - Duplicate primitive-root/fixing/congruence/power-action helpers removed
    from TraceNormBound and reused from Author D's compiled TowerDefinition.
    The whole-group adapter reuses Author D's InfiniteImage finishing theorem;
    its copied TH0 arithmetic block is removed.

UPSTREAM_ATTRIBUTION.md is the upstream attribution document recovered by
this task's scout. UPSTREAM_NOTICE preserves the upstream NOTICE (its first
80 lines), together with the pre-existing Z-in-Q vendor annex carried by the
copy used here. That older annex describes earlier vendor integrations,
not the modifications listed above.

Original supporting modules written for W11:
  AlgebraicTrace.lean, Tower.lean, ContinuousTrace.lean, Equivariance.lean,
  TraceComparison.lean, CyclotomicBounds.lean.
They reuse Mathlib normalized trace and normed completion, and the vendored
Tau Ceti cyclotomic root-adjoin/character theorems. Mathlib and Tau Ceti are
Apache-2.0; their author and provenance notices remain in their source files.

Mathematical references read:
  J. Tate, p-divisible groups, Proc. Conf. Local Fields (Driebergen 1966),
  Springer 1967, printed pp. 170-174, especially Proposition 5, Corollary 3,
  Proposition 6 with its base-shift remark, and the continuous trace on p. 173.
